1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,210
Good morning everyone.

2
00:00:03,210 --> 00:00:10,380
So today we're going to look at an important creative activity and that's hand knitting.

3
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:15,694
Ancient knitted garments have been found in many different countries,

4
00:00:15,694 --> 00:00:21,540
showing that knitting is a global activity with a long history.

5
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:28,187
When someone says the word 'knitting' we might well picture an elderly person -

6
00:00:28,187 --> 00:00:36,880
a grandmother perhaps - sitting by the fire knitting garments for themselves or other members of the family.

7
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:46,078
It's a homely image, but one that may lead you to feel that knitting is an activity of the past - and,

8
00:00:46,078 --> 00:00:48,420
indeed, during the previous decade

9
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:54,400
it was one of the skills that was predicted to vanish from everyday life.

10
00:00:54,400 --> 00:01:02,065
For although humans have sewn and knitted their own clothing for a very long time,

11
00:01:02,065 --> 00:01:06,240
many of these craft-based skills went into decline

12
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:08,707
when industrial machines took over -

13
00:01:08,707 --> 00:01:15,350
mainly because they were no longer passed down from one generation to another.

14
00:01:15,350 --> 00:01:24,339
However, that's all changing and interest in knitting classes in many countries is actually rising,

15
00:01:24,339 --> 00:01:31,530
as more and more people are seeking formal instruction in the skill.

16
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:39,480
With that trend, we're also seeing an increase in the sales figures for knitting equipment.

17
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:45,406
So why do people want to be taught to knit at a time

18
00:01:45,486 --> 00:01:48,720
when a machine can readily do the job for them

19
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:53,340
The answer is that knitting, as a handicraft

20
00:01:53,340 --> 00:01:56,290
has numerous benefits for those doing it.

21
00:01:56,290 --> 00:02:00,630
Let's consider what some of these might be.

22
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:04,740
While many people knitted garments in the past

23
00:02:04,740 --> 00:02:08,358
because they couldn't afford to buy clothes,

24
00:02:08,358 --> 00:02:12,100
it's still true today that knitting can be helpful

25
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:15,570
if you're experiencing economic hardship.

26
00:02:15,570 --> 00:02:21,620
If you have several children who all need warm winter clothes

27
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:25,010
knitting may save you a lot of money.

28
00:02:25,010 --> 00:02:30,766
And the results of knitting your own clothes can be very rewarding,

29
00:02:30,766 --> 00:02:36,940
even though the skills you need to get going are really quite basic

30
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:39,880
and the financial outlay is minimal.

31
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:47,300
But the more significant benefits in today's world are to do with well-being.

32
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:54,609
In a world where it's estimated that we spend up to nine hours a day online,

33
00:02:54,609 --> 00:03:00,090
doing something with our hands that is craft-based makes us feel good.

34
00:03:00,090 --> 00:03:10,610
It releases us from the stress of a technological, fast-paced life.

35
00:03:10,610 --> 00:03:16,410
Now, let's look back a bit to early knitting activities.

36
00:03:16,410 --> 00:03:21,945
In fact, no one really knows when knitting first began,

37
00:03:21,945 --> 00:03:29,140
but archaeological remains have disclosed plenty of information for us to think about.

38
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:44,780
One of the interesting things about knitting is that the earliest pieces of clothing that have been found suggest that most of the items produced were round rather than flat.

39
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:52,734
Discoveries from the 3rd and 4th centuries in Egypt show that things like socks and gloves,

40
00:03:52,734 --> 00:03:57,020
that were needed to keep hands and feet warm

41
00:03:57,020 --> 00:04:02,180
were knitted in one piece using four or five needles.

42
00:04:02,180 --> 00:04:09,130
That's very different from most knitting patterns today, which only require two.

43
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:18,998
What's more, the very first needles people used were hand carved out of wood and other natural materials,

44
00:04:18,998 --> 00:04:25,578
like bone, whereas today's needles are largely made of steel or plastic

45
00:04:25,578 --> 00:04:31,060
and make that characteristic clicking sound when someone's using them.

46
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:35,818
Ancient people knitted using yarns made from linen,

47
00:04:35,818 --> 00:04:43,550
hemp, cotton and wool, and these were often very rough on the skin.

48
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:48,520
The spinning wheel, which allowed people to make finer yarns

49
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:51,381
and produce much greater quantities of them,

50
00:04:51,381 --> 00:04:55,760
led to the dominance of wool in the knitting industry

51
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:58,290
often favoured for its warmth.

52
00:04:58,290 --> 00:05:05,081
Another interesting fact about knitting is that because it was practised in

53
00:05:05,081 --> 00:05:09,700
so many parts of the world for so many purposes

54
00:05:10,020 --> 00:05:13,570
regional differences in style developed.

55
00:05:13,570 --> 00:05:23,703
This visual identity has allowed researchers to match bits of knitted clothing that have been unearthed over time to the region from

56
00:05:23,703 --> 00:05:29,230
which the wearer came or the job that he or she did.

57
00:05:29,230 --> 00:05:39,400
As I've mentioned, knitting offered people from poor communities a way of making extra money while doing other tasks.

58
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:42,780
For many centuries, it seems, men

59
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:47,199
women and children took every opportunity to knit,

60
00:05:47,199 --> 00:05:54,440
for example, while watching over sheep, walking to market or riding in boats.

61
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:59,000
So, let's move on to take a...
